WEBVTT

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.430
At last, the tournament finals...

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:12.440
We've really made it this far, huh?

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:14.670
Of course, Brother!

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.100
That's right! It means you've 
all got that level of ability.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:20.170
Mm-hm!

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:24.040
So, everyone, have confidence in 
yourselves, relax, and let's go!

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:25.620
Huh?

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:27.620
Huh?!

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.770
P-Please wait for me!

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.920
Shin is the one who's worried the most.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:40.170
Thanks to everyone, I was able to come here.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.320
Together with these friends, 
I'll do my very best

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:46.360
here at these finals!

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:22.960
Vanguard National Championship
Tournament Finals

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.030
As expected, everyone else looks formidable.

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.750
That's the Hiroshima team, Wonder Boys!

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.550
The Osaka team, Wild Angel!

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:35.850
The Kumamoto team, Southern 
Winds, is here, too!

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:39.650
I've seen all of these teams 
before in Monthly Vanguard!

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:42.780
In other words, these teams are all so 
strong, they appear in the magazine.

00:02:44.810 --> 00:02:47.840
Huh? Misaki, are you scared?

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:51.110
What are you talking about? This 
is just trembling from excitement!

00:02:52.230 --> 00:02:55.920
Me too! I'm trampling with excitement!

00:02:56.420 --> 00:02:58.290
Hi, Q4!

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.860
Team Caesar!

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.090
Team Caesar?!

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:05.350
The ones who took second place last time?!

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:06.480
Huh?

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:09.480
I hate standing out!

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.900
Mr. Mitsusada...

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:16.860
The Battle Begins! Tournament Finals

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:20.840
Koutei is always like this. Yeesh...

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.570
But it fits Mr. Mitsusada's personality.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:29.350
Aichi, something about you seems to
have changed again since the preliminaries?

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.550
Oh...

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:36.560
It's like you're back to normal... 
Yeah. I like this Aichi better.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:38.480
Thank you.

00:03:38.860 --> 00:03:41.560
I saw video recordings of you 
at the preliminary rounds.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:42.590
Impressive as usual.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:46.100
You Q4 guys are the ones who've 
really upped your game.

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.800
You've improved a lot since our 
training camp over the summer.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.150
At the time, we thought...

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:57.060
...that Q4 would become our rival.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:57.810
And then...

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.930
...seeing you at the elimination 
rounds made us certain of it.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.220
Mr. Mitsusada...

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:06.520
I'm really looking forward 
to fighting you guys here.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:09.290
Right back at ya!

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:11.770
But we're gonna beat you!

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:14.510
We're not gonna lose either!

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:17.380
Let's all fight to the best of our abilities!

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:18.220
Right!

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.720
Young lions, who have been selected 
from all over the country...

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.730
Young hawks, who are flapping your wings...

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:28.240
You are the true Vanguards!

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:31.070
Thank you for your patience, everyone!

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.190
The Vanguard Championship...

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:35.220
...Tournament Finals...

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:36.850
...has begun!

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:41.560
At last!

00:04:41.560 --> 00:04:43.630
Kourin!

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.040
Well, we'll see you on the field...

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.200
Right!

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:00.090
Gathered here today

00:05:00.090 --> 00:05:02.310
are the 16 strongest teams 
from across the country!

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:07.160
So let's start with a big round of applause 
for these young lions and young hawks!

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:09.520
You're all great!

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:10.810
The tension is rising...

00:05:10.960 --> 00:05:14.940
And now we'll explain the 
progression of the matches!

00:05:14.940 --> 00:05:18.730
Unlike the preliminary rounds, the 
finals uses a knockout competition.

00:05:20.070 --> 00:05:22.850
So today, there'll be the 
first round, the second round,

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:25.540
all the way up to 14, the semifinal.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:28.030
And then, the last two teams left...

00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:30.290
...will be able to challenge each other...

00:05:30.610 --> 00:05:33.030
...here tomorrow, at the final battle!

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:35.490
And the winning team...

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:40.790
...will gain what everyone wants! What 
everyone desires! What everyone longs for!

00:05:41.120 --> 00:05:47.220
That Vanguard team will earn the 
title of "the country's strongest"!

00:05:47.940 --> 00:05:52.410
Everyone, do you wanna see the 
number one national Vanguard team?!

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:54.800
I can't hear you!

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:57.750
Everyone, everyone, everyone, 
everyone! Let's make some noise!

00:05:58.050 --> 00:06:02.350
Do you wanna see the number one 
Vanguard team in the country?!

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:06.540
Okay, everyone! Thank you!

00:06:06.950 --> 00:06:09.360
Next up is the pledge for fair play.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:13.740
The person to give it is the leader 
of the team that won last time,

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:16.880
and who will participate this time as well...

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:23.120
...Team Foo Fighter AL4's Ren Suzugamori!

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:48.230
Everyone who is going to fight in the finals,

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.500
congratulations on getting this far...

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:55.170
...even though your chances 
of winning are zero.

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:06.360
The members of my team, AL4, 
are incomparably strong.

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:12.750
But more than anything, I have a special 
power that only the chosen possess.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:20.640
That power subdues and humiliates everyone.

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:24.990
Nothing pleases me more than seeing that.

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:27.920
Victory belongs to me and AL4...

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:30.750
...no matter how hard everyone tries.

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:34.200
But please entertain me with 
your pointless struggles.

00:07:36.430 --> 00:07:40.280
This has been Ren Suzugamori's 
pledge for fair play.

00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:43.040
Hey, you!

00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:45.900
Wait, Kourin! We're on stage!

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:53.490
Whoa! Aichi sure got called out!

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:56.450
No, I'm pretty sure we were 
all included in that...

00:07:56.450 --> 00:08:00.480
Man, that guy's a first-class 
arrogant jerk...

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:02.330
What does "arrogant" mean?

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:05.390
Oh, a person who thinks, "I'm 
the Lord of heaven and earth."

00:08:05.390 --> 00:08:07.970
Someone who's incredibly self-important.

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:09.970
What was that about "heaven and earth"?

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:13.620
Never mind, not important. 
But you need to study more.

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:23.910
Ren...

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.920
Aichi Sendou...

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:32.100
What do you want? This is odd. 
I have no business with you.

00:08:35.690 --> 00:08:40.650
Don't tell me you've changed your foolish mind 
and want to accept my invitation to Foo Fighter?

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:43.390
I...

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.340
...don't want to become like you.

00:08:46.460 --> 00:08:47.390
What?

00:08:56.030 --> 00:08:57.920
I'm returning this.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:03.790
Certainly, the power of Psyqualia is amazing.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:06.390
But I'm not going to get addicted to it.

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:12.470
Vanguard fighting isn't about subduing 
people or anything like that.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:15.460
If you do that, you're sure 
to lose something precious.

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:25.800
I'm going to stick with a Vanguard 
fight that's different from yours.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:29.420
Then I'm going to fight you and win.

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:48.470
What the heck was that?!

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:50.130
You've pushed your luck far enough!

00:09:50.410 --> 00:09:53.300
That's what a newbie gets 
for trying to show off!

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.750
I hate everything about you people!

00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:01.340
I can't wait to fight you! I'll 
beat you to rithersmeens!  {sic}

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.470
Amusing. This should be fun.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:14.470
Aichi...

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:19.560
I <i>will</i> make you regret becoming my enemy.

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:32.520
You still had that deck?

00:10:33.210 --> 00:10:38.510
Even if it was only for a short time, these 
units were also allies that fought with me.

00:10:39.120 --> 00:10:43.790
Um... Er... Uh... Er... Ah...

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:48.000
You look kind of happy, Kourin.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:52.260
But can he win the finals 
without Shadow Paladin?

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.130
A-Ahem...

00:10:54.130 --> 00:10:57.520
Well, everyone's fired up, 
here, there and everywhere!

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:00.870
So let's announce the 
pairings of the first match!

00:11:06.190 --> 00:11:07.980
We're in the first match!

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:11.010
All right! I'm more pumped up 
now than I'd be having to wait!

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:13.260
AL4 is...

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:19.690
So if you don't win through to the final 
round, you won't be able to fight them.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:24.240
Until we're face to face with them in the 
final, let's show 'em what we can do!

00:11:24.500 --> 00:11:28.800
We'll show 'em that our Vanguard 
fight is different than theirs!

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:34.970
Okay! I'll go first!

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:36.670
I want to be second.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:37.220
Then...

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:40.280
I'm not going to fight.

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:44.480
You three won the preliminary rounds.

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:46.720
Just the three of you will handle this tournament, too.

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:50.010
What do you mean?

00:11:50.010 --> 00:11:52.530
I'll translate. What he means is...

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:55.210
You three together made it 
this far on your strength.

00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:59.520
So you three should also accept the 
honor of fighting at the finals.

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:01.940
That's what you meant, isn't it, Kai?

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:07.310
Huh, that's what you were trying to say? 
As always, you come across clear as mud!

00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:09.490
I'll do my best, Kai!

00:12:10.260 --> 00:12:11.920
Well... Good luck.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:25.950
Please watch our Vanguard fight.

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:40.390
The National Vanguard Championship!

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:42.470
The first round of the tournament finals!

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:42.470
Team Q4 vs Team Wonder Boy

00:12:42.890 --> 00:12:44.300
Start!

00:12:46.700 --> 00:12:49.120
I'm gonna win this showdown for sure!

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:59.480
Who is this guy?!

00:13:01.610 --> 00:13:03.780
The winner: Kamui Katsuragi!

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:06.100
That's our Kamui!

00:13:10.610 --> 00:13:12.240
Here! Here's where I win it!

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:22.710
The winner: Misaki Tokura!

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:26.120
Team Q4 has won their first two matches!

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:27.630
Then they move up!

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:28.850
All right!

00:13:28.850 --> 00:13:29.860
Yay!

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:32.490
I'd expect no less from my pupils!

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:33.500
Hey...

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:35.990
Third Fight
Team Caesar vs Team Southern Winds

00:13:34.340 --> 00:13:40.790
Next up, the first match in the third fight, 
Team Caesar versus Team Southern Winds!

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:44.170
The curtain is cl-<i>o</i>-sing in the seventh turn!

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.400
Go, Enigman Storm!

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:51.920
This is so frustrating!

00:13:52.370 --> 00:13:54.810
The winner: Kenji Mitsusada!

00:13:57.660 --> 00:14:00.060
Mr. Mitsusada really is strong!

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:01.960
That's Team Caesar for you.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:06.170
We're not gonna lose either!

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:12.870
The first fight of the second round, 
Team Q4 versus Team Wild Angel!

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:15.400
The end of this first match 
is about to be decided!

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:21.870
Grand Spinning Destruction!

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.560
The winner: Kamui Katsuragi!

00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:33.730
I have shields worth 20000 in my hand.

00:14:33.730 --> 00:14:36.720
25000 if I use a card to intercept...

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:39.830
I should be able to withstand her attack!

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:44.600
Final Turn!

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:45.620
What?!

00:14:46.840 --> 00:14:49.320
Beaming beautiful goddess.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:51.810
I ride CEO Amaterasu!

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:57.680
With Amaterasu's skill, I get +4000 power!

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.830
And one more skill, Soulcharge!

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:04.370
Then I check the top card of my deck...

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:05.530
...and call!

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:09.890
With the skill of White Hare of Inaba, 
I put one card from my hand into the Soul.

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:12.980
What?!

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:15.760
Looks like you've figured it 
out. With a boost from Gemini...

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:19.980
...Battle Maiden, Tagitsuhime 
attacks Maiden of Trailing Rose!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:25.120
If there are six or more cards in 
the Soul when Tagitsuhime attacks...

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:28.260
That's right. And there are 
exactly six cards in my Soul.

00:15:28.820 --> 00:15:31.160
Tagitsuhime receives +3000 power!

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:34.500
Yes! That's 20000 power!

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:35.700
But it's only a grade 2...

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:38.350
Still, there's one more Tagitsuhime!

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:42.130
With this, all three of her 
attacks are over 20000 power!

00:15:42.220 --> 00:15:43.420
Not bad, sister!

00:15:44.050 --> 00:15:47.270
That's rough requesting for 15000 in shields every time!

00:15:47.270 --> 00:15:48.940
Misaki is doing great!

00:15:50.990 --> 00:15:52.710
I guard with Sweet Honey!

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:55.890
And then I intercept with 
Knight of Young Leaves, Gene!

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:59.490
Yes! At 20000 to 25000, the 
attack won't go through!

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:01.750
With a boost from White Hare of Inaba,

00:16:02.130 --> 00:16:03.660
Amaterasu attacks!

00:16:05.280 --> 00:16:06.660
No guard!

00:16:07.180 --> 00:16:08.560
Twin drive check...

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:10.110
Heal trigger?!

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:12.250
I heal 1 point of damage.

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:14.580
I give the power to the Tagitsuhime 
that hasn't attacked yet.

00:16:20.210 --> 00:16:20.920
Tagitsuhime!

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:29.820
The winner: Misaki Tokura!

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:34.140
Team Q4 advances to the semifinals!

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:37.720
You've got some real skills there.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:38.950
Thank you.

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:41.900
Maybe we can put our hopes on your team...

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:43.290
What do you mean?

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:44.400
Those jerks!

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:51.780
They destroyed everyone's mood 
with those opening remarks!

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:54.070
Will you make them pay, for everyone?

00:16:54.960 --> 00:16:56.340
Leave it to us.

00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:58.810
I'm counting on you.

00:16:59.480 --> 00:17:02.640
All right, that's the end 
of the second-round fights!

00:17:02.640 --> 00:17:04.000
The surviving teams are...

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:05.880
...these four!

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:06.200
Team Q4
Team FFBS
Team Caesar
Team FFAL4

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:10.520
Of course, AL4 is still 
around... but BS too, huh?

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:12.520
And Team Caesar...

00:17:12.920 --> 00:17:15.950
And the fight pairings are...

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:16.520
...here!

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:21.040
Semifinals First Fight
Team FFBS versus Team FFAL4

00:17:21.090 --> 00:17:24.040
The first fight is BS and AL4?!

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:25.540
Allies against each other!

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:29.140
More importantly, let's pay attention 
to what's in front of us!

00:17:29.800 --> 00:17:31.800
Semifinals Second Fight
Team Q4 versus Team Caesar

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:33.780
Team Caesar!

00:17:39.010 --> 00:17:41.380
All right... the first, noteworthy fight

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:43.570
of the semifinals...

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:44.870
...start!

00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:48.670
That's the end of my turn!

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:58.860
Even though I was almost there... Even 
though I absolutely had to win here...

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:04.640
Losing to Team Q4 is a blunder 
that I can't tolerate.

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:10.240
But I am a generous person.

00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:15.560
If even one of you shows 
the ability to beat AL4,

00:18:15.560 --> 00:18:18.510
it will redeem you as a 
member of Foo Fighter,

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:20.280
and your error will be 
water under the bridge.

00:18:21.020 --> 00:18:23.800
R-Really?! Thank you!

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:30.670
Final Turn!

00:18:32.540 --> 00:18:34.570
A Final Turn declaration?!

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:35.730
I see...

00:18:36.570 --> 00:18:38.960
Think back to the previous turn.

00:18:38.960 --> 00:18:42.390
He guarded twice with Dark Soul Conductor.

00:18:42.980 --> 00:18:44.630
Conductor's skill.

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:48.130
When the guard is finished and 
it moves to the Drop Zone,

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:49.740
I can do two Soulcharges!

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:56.380
He used that guard twice, put four more 
cards into the soul, and so now...

00:18:56.870 --> 00:18:58.940
There are thirteen cards in the Soul!

00:18:58.940 --> 00:19:00.670
That's gonna be the clinching move.

00:19:02.100 --> 00:19:02.850
I call...

00:19:09.230 --> 00:19:11.010
Stil Vampir!

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:14.940
No, what we should be paying attention 
to here is Demon of Aspiration, Amon.

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:20.950
With Demon of Aspiration, Amon's skill, if there are six 
or more cards in the Soul, it gets +3000 power.

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:24.050
And on top of that, with Demon 
World Marquis, Amon's skill,

00:19:24.050 --> 00:19:26.960
it gets +1000 power for 
every card in the Soul.

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:30.600
That's 23000 power!

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:33.510
It's the result of being so desperate 
to attack during the last turn.

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:35.510
He let his opponent's Soul fill up.

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:38.120
He underestimated Tetsu.

00:19:38.590 --> 00:19:43.190
With a boost from Prisoner Beast, 
I attack with Demon of Aspiration, Amon.

00:19:47.510 --> 00:19:51.630
Demon World Marquis, Amon attacks 
with a boost from Alluring Succubus!

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:03.240
The winner of the first 
match of the semifinals...

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:05.390
...is Tetsu Shinjou!

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:08.960
He didn't go easy on his 
fellow Foo Fighter, huh?

00:20:13.510 --> 00:20:15.760
I'm finishing this with Barking Manticore!

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:27.030
The winner: Asaka Narumi!

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:32.810
The winner of the first fight 
of the semifinals is Team AL4!

00:20:41.030 --> 00:20:42.530
Kyou Yahagi!

00:20:43.600 --> 00:20:46.580
Jeez, there's nothing beautiful about that!

00:20:46.580 --> 00:20:49.800
Now you're the same as me!

00:20:57.280 --> 00:21:02.010
Giving hope to the weak, then 
trampling it underfoot...

00:21:02.690 --> 00:21:05.220
There's nothing more delicious than that.

00:21:07.230 --> 00:21:09.650
If you do that, you're sure 
to lose something precious.

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:14.130
Stupid... Nonsense...

00:21:22.270 --> 00:21:25.350
Tetsu and Asaka really are terrific, too...

00:21:25.350 --> 00:21:27.440
They may be even stronger than before.

00:21:28.030 --> 00:21:32.160
All right, before you steel 
yourselves for that...

00:21:40.160 --> 00:21:42.390
We're both good rivals for each other.

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:44.360
Let's fight without reserve!

00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:48.400
We're gonna give it all we've got!

00:21:49.900 --> 00:21:54.340
All right, next up is the second 
fight of the semifinals...

00:21:54.340 --> 00:21:58.650
Opposing each other... 
Team Q4 and Team Caesar!

00:22:08.700 --> 00:22:11.290
Let's see how good you really are...

00:22:12.510 --> 00:22:13.580
...Aichi.

00:23:50.960 --> 00:23:54.080
The tournament finals! I'm totally nervous!

00:23:54.080 --> 00:23:57.350
Ren Suzugamori didn't 
participate in the AL4 fight.

00:23:57.340 --> 00:23:58.240
Asaka Narumi...

00:23:58.360 --> 00:23:59.930
...and Tetsu Shinjou...

00:23:59.930 --> 00:24:01.500
Yeah, they really are incredible!

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:03.340
Certainly, our goal is AL4, but...

00:24:03.340 --> 00:24:04.840
I know, Brother!

00:24:04.840 --> 00:24:06.600
Before that, Team Caesar!

00:24:06.600 --> 00:24:09.240
I intend to go in thinking that I'm 
practicing with a partner with higher skills!

00:24:09.240 --> 00:24:11.400
Caesar, I'm gonna hit you 
with everything I've got!

00:24:11.400 --> 00:24:13.130
Next time: Gladiator!

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:14.900
Kamui, Misaki...

00:24:14.900 --> 00:24:17.060
Let's picture it! Us, doing our best!

00:24:17.060 --> 00:24:18.040
Yeah!
